        "original_id": "a579dd4e-940b-538a-a52d-7395ac4788f8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Toyota Owners 400, Federated Auto Parts 400\n- Companies: Crown Royal, Diageo, Seagram\n- Places: Richmond Raceway, Richmond, Virginia, Daytona Speedweeks\n- Topics: NASCAR Cup Series title sponsorship, essay contest naming\n\nFacts:\n- In 2000, Diageo acquired Crown Royal when the Seagram portfolio was dissolved.\n- Crown Royal is a blended Canadian whisky.\n- From 2007 to 2011, Crown Royal, a former title sponsor of the Toyota Owners 400, named that race after the winner of an essay contest during Daytona Speedweeks.\n- The Federated Auto Parts 400 is an annual Monster Energy NASCAR Cup Series stock car race held at Richmond Raceway in Richmond, Virginia.\n- The Federated Auto Parts 400 is the second of two Richmond Raceway NASCAR Cup Series races each year, with the Toyota Owners 400 held in the spring as the first race.",
